  "commits": [
    {
      "sha": "ced2ee55f5d1c7b7cb29bc08ba451b2070138d52",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/ced2ee55f5d1c7b7cb29bc08ba451b2070138d52",
      "message": "Select the testing deployment profile for CI migration\n\nThe isolated migration starts the node CLI after building it and must provide the deployment profile required by configuration. Bind that step to the preprod-testing artifact and existing Preprod network rather than weakening the profile requirement.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-03T09:17:29Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "c0d9289195a9ece1d80e542db8370876082d03f6",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/c0d9289195a9ece1d80e542db8370876082d03f6",
      "message": "Bind watcher CI authority smoke to the built profile\n\nThe shipped public sample uses depth 30 while the testing image requires depth 3. Generate the disposable smoke policy from the compiled profile and recompute its digest so the strict authority parser and authenticated HTTP smoke can run.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-03T09:00:33Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "18b65d58bfad9aad6973b8a01b2573acc144599a",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/18b65d58bfad9aad6973b8a01b2573acc144599a",
      "message": "Ratchet module size limits after shared recovery cleanup\n\nThe field lifecycle and e2e summary cleanup reduced their modules to 907 and 608 lines. Lower the stale 949 and 627 exceptions so Repository Tools CI enforces the current sizes without unused headroom.\n\nRefs #740",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-03T08:47:59Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "aa7db4dfb66951636d58190ab277eb356cdb659c",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/aa7db4dfb66951636d58190ab277eb356cdb659c",
      "message": "Carry current queue targets through shared removal actions (#740)\n\nRequire every typed family removal action to retain the authenticated current target alongside its immediate child and permanent proof reference. Carry the field through observation, planning and capture; update callers in place without a fallback. Preserve the obsolete-runner deletion and strict signed input checks.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-03T05:03:43Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "6811b7489292fdbef5415ea15ef6117942dcd14a",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/6811b7489292fdbef5415ea15ef6117942dcd14a",
      "message": "Split required-gate summary tests without changing behavior\n\nMove two unchanged test registrations into an imported helper to satisfy the canonical file line limit. Keep assertions and registration order identical.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-03T04:29:17Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "c6456379c757cc7d659c60c855e69e430f39ff28",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/c6456379c757cc7d659c60c855e69e430f39ff28",
      "message": "Replace obsolete field runner with shared recovery (#740)\n\nRemove the family-specific journal, orchestration and exports. Shared recovery authenticates descendant removal receipts and resumes already-slashed cleanup from the durable workflow journal. Retain evidence checks, transaction builders and validators.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-03T04:24:45Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "0eb45602c5eb2f9a2d54d7369e6cb2186388bc93",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/0eb45602c5eb2f9a2d54d7369e6cb2186388bc93",
      "message": "Fit canonical output proof roles within the publication budget\n\nKeep the original descriptor decoder unchanged and specialize its canonical schema parser at the two measured oversized consumers. Share the value-fold successor checks while preserving guards, parameter schemas, and the existing publication limit.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-03T02:48:03Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "b00a34cb60eac329616b4c8b305c63fafdf4e390",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/b00a34cb60eac329616b4c8b305c63fafdf4e390",
      "message": "Pay the authenticated prover when any caller submits slashing (#643)\n\nBind removal rewards to the authenticated proof producer across descendant removals and active or retired operators. Permit a different wallet to submit without requiring the prover signature, and retain validated reward attribution through funding recovery.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-03T02:36:33Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "b285d1271142384fcfc8c7e51fff8e204367cf22",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/b285d1271142384fcfc8c7e51fff8e204367cf22",
      "message": "Resolve compatible CBOR peers for Lucid reference script sweeps (#647)\n\nPin the older Lucid utilities peer graph to CBOR 1.6.6 while retaining CBOR 2 for the newer direct UPLC and Data libraries. The unchanged five reference-script sweep scenarios failed before and pass with the repaired graph; the root composed ten-case history and sweep suite passes. Frozen offline installation passes.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-03T00:52:17Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "c89fe0059312a9b70194cb5a0ae1694f342e12bd",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/c89fe0059312a9b70194cb5a0ae1694f342e12bd",
      "message": "Pin the native deep Data decoder and profile-bound watcher smoke\n\nUse the earliest upstream decoder release that accepts supported deep Data without a local parser shim, and keep the Go build pins consistent. Bind the disposable authority smoke configuration to the compiled testing profile while retaining public depth-30 templates and strict policy checks.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-03T00:27:10Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "31df81fe3cbd7da4987e689304e51a528dc49d78",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/31df81fe3cbd7da4987e689304e51a528dc49d78",
      "message": "Bound node declaration build heap to avoid CI worker exhaustion\n\nThe tsup declaration worker exhausts its default heap during clean CI builds. Give both build steps the measured 6144 MiB heap while preserving inherited Node options; runtime image options remain unchanged.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-03T00:07:47Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "86541d2b4e9a45a243473f09e749dc6956be436f",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/86541d2b4e9a45a243473f09e749dc6956be436f",
      "message": "Fix typed byte buffers and external source references\n\nUse the declared Uint8Array return values in the Plutus test helpers and keep external Cardano source names out of local documentation link checks.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-02T23:48:22Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "f2ad2a7963bf7b47d9ae355464a6a6c2ad1d00fb",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/f2ad2a7963bf7b47d9ae355464a6a6c2ad1d00fb",
      "message": "Check blueprint application against the pinned UPLC oracle\n\nUse the independently supplied Plutus Data parameters with the pinned WASM evaluator. The previous direct Lucid comparison crashes in its upstream Harmonic encoder before checking the application boundary. Keep all existing arity, schema, cache and validator identity assertions.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-02T23:08:25Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "c3eac53e9b88ce41923c865c0244c4d49a130166",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/c3eac53e9b88ce41923c865c0244c4d49a130166",
      "message": "Preserve the exact DA MPF package with reproducible source\n\nKeep the reviewed DA node-encoding package installable without relying on an unpublished package commit. Preserve its exact archive, genuine modified source, locked build dependencies, member receipts and reproduction recipe through the existing vendored dependency model.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-02T22:43:42Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "bd9959c7cfaa1436b0e3192ae835d71c61f24950",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/bd9959c7cfaa1436b0e3192ae835d71c61f24950",
      "message": "Plan public preprod acceptance against the October deadline\n\nWork backward from October 31 with integration, review and public-profile lifecycle milestones. Keep readiness gates open, distinguish ticket counts from acceptance work, and label unconfirmed capacity and ownership.\n\nVerification on 2026-10-02 in the isolated documentation worktree: node scripts/preflight.mjs --base 4d9d200cc4dc3b169ea6dbffc6b3426c9c51993c --json passed all 8 selected checks, exit 0. Prettier --check and git diff --check passed, exit 0. Live GitHub states and a local count check confirmed 65 gates, 28 open epic children out of 31, and 21 weekdays. Application tests and live public acceptance were not rerun for this documentation-only plan. Refs #696 and #724.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-10-02T07:27:30Z"
    }
  ],
